# Step 1: Generate interaction features representing more complex relationships
# Feature name: loc_d_interaction
# Feature description: This feature captures the interaction between loc (lines of code) and d (Halstead difficulty). It is computed as loc * d.
# Usefulness: Defect-prone modules may potentially have high difficulty (d) when paired with complex codebases (loc). By explicitly capturing this interaction, the model might better differentiate between complex, defect-prone modules and those that are simple and less error-prone.
df['loc_d_interaction'] = df['loc'] * df['d']
end

python
