# Feature name: modularity_ratio
# Feature description: This feature is computed as iv(g) / (v(g) + 1), which captures the design complexity iv(g) relative to cyclomatic complexity v(g).
# Usefulness: iv(g) and v(g) both measure structural complexity, but the ratio might help the model better distinguish tightly coupled or modular code. Poor modularity is often linked with a higher chance of defects in software engineering.
df['modularity_ratio'] = df['iv(g)'] / (df['v(g)'] + 1)
end

